{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788190543,"nonce":"PHP+G2nFhTGCLzUDbzRCFSq46Gw=","title":"orders claims read-only but mutates: missing FloatMenuMakerMap.makingFor causes a colony-wide bill cooldown, an RNG burn and a fidelity divergence","message":"Found by investigation 2026-08-31, CONFIRMED in decompiled 1.6 source. Not yet\nreproduced on the bench — see the acceptance below.\n\n`PawnOrderVerbs.cs` `ScanWorkGivers` is documented \"Read-only: no job is taken\",\nand the `orders` verb's own result note tells the agent the same. **It is not\nread-only.** It runs `scanner.HasJobOnThing` / `JobOnThing` with `forced:true`\nacross every `WorkGiverDef`, and — unlike the vanilla path it claims parity\nwith — it never sets `FloatMenuMakerMap.makingFor`.\n\n`RimWorld/FloatMenuMakerMap.cs` sets `makingFor = context.FirstSelectedPawn`\naround its whole option-building pass and nulls it after. Four consequences of\nnot doing so, each CONFIRMED by reading the member named:\n\n1. **A colony-wide bill cooldown.** `RimWorld/WorkGiver_DoBill.cs`\n   `StartOrResumeBillJob` takes its `makingFor != pawn` branch and writes\n   `bill.nextTickToSearchForIngredients = TicksGame + IntRange(500,600)\n   .RandomInRange`. That suppresses the bill for the WHOLE COLONY. So calling\n   `orders` on a stove can stop the colony cooking for ~10 in-game seconds. A\n   player's click never does this.\n2. **An RNG burn.** That same line advances the shared `Rand` stream —\n   `WorldSafe`'s Class R hazard, which this project already treats as\n   disqualifying for an observer.\n3. **A fidelity divergence from the menu it reproduces.** `Verse/DangerUtility.cs`\n   `NormalMaxDanger` returns `Danger.Deadly` when `makingFor == p`. Without it,\n   `orders` evaluates reachability at a DIFFERENT danger threshold than the\n   float menu, so it can honestly disagree with the game's own answer — the\n   exact failure the widget-parity doctrine exists to prevent.\n4. **Missing reasons.** The \"you're missing 30 steel\" `JobFailReason` strings are\n   only produced when `makingFor == pawn`. Today `orders` gets a silent skip\n   where the player gets a reason, costing the agent a round trip to find out\n   why.\n\nTHE FIX IS ONE LINE plus a try/finally: set `FloatMenuMakerMap.makingFor = pawn`\naround the scan and null it after, exactly as vanilla does. That closes a state\nmutation, an RNG burn, a fidelity gap and a missing-reason gap together.\n\nWHAT THE FIX DOES NOT CLOSE, and should be documented rather than dodged:\n`WorkGiver_DoBill.JobOnThing` also calls `billGiver.BillStack\n.RemoveIncompletableBills()`, which does `bills.Remove(bill)` +\n`Notify_BillDeleted(bill)` — **it deletes bills** — and that fires with or\nwithout `makingFor`. It is genuine click-parity (the player's menu does it too),\nso it belongs in the verb's header as a disclosed side effect of asking, not as\nsomething to suppress.\n\nAlso worth recording: every non-null `JobOnThing` pops `SimplePool\u003cJob\u003e` and\nincrements `UniqueIDsManager.nextJobID`, **which is scribed** — so a probe job\npermanently inflates a saved counter. Harmless, but it means \"read-only\" was\nnever strictly true for this verb and the header should stop claiming it.\n\nSCOPE NOTE: `WorkGiverDef.directOrderable` defaults true, so `ScanWorkGivers`\nalready runs arbitrary THIRD-PARTY `JobOnThing` implementations on a 38-mod\nbench. Vanilla's own worst case is destructive; there is no basis for assuming\nmods are better behaved and no practical way to audit them all. That is an\nargument for the disclosure in the header, not for removing the verb.\n\nAcceptance\n\n- `FloatMenuMakerMap.makingFor` is set around the scan in a try/finally, cited\n  by FILE + MEMBER against `RimWorld/FloatMenuMakerMap.cs`.\n- **Reproduce the bug first, then show it fixed:** read a bill's\n  `nextTickToSearchForIngredients` on a stove, call `orders` against that stove,\n  read it again — it moves by 500-600 before the fix and does not after.\n- A `JobFailReason` string that was previously blank now comes back populated\n  for an ingredient-starved bill.\n- The verb's header and its result note stop claiming \"read-only\" and instead\n  disclose what asking costs: `RemoveIncompletableBills` may delete a bill whose\n  body part is gone, and a job id is consumed per candidate.","files":null}]}